---
import contract from '../data/contract.json';

const labels = {
  guide: 'Wire contract guide',
  request: 'Request envelope schema',
  response: 'Response envelope schema',
  payload_pins: 'External payload pins',
};
---
<section id="contract" aria-labelledby="contract-title">
  <h2 id="contract-title">Contract source</h2>
  <p>
    These references point to an unreleased source snapshot of <code>logifos-rs</code>,
    revision <code>{contract.revision}</code>. It specifies a target contract;
    it is not a release or an implemented renderer. This site keeps no schema copies.
  </p>
  <ul>
    {Object.entries(contract.references).map(([key, path]) => (
      <li><a data-contract-reference={key} href={`${contract.repository}/blob/${contract.revision}/${path}`}>{labels[key as keyof typeof labels]}</a></li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p>
    The target ABI version is <span data-contract-version="abi">{contract.abi_version}</span>;
    the target JSON schema version is <span data-contract-version="schema">{contract.schema_version}</span>.
    Neither number is a package version. Formula and MathML syntax payload pins
    remain unresolved in this snapshot, so successful payload qualification is blocked.
  </p>
  <p>
    Once a release is qualified, these references are planned to follow its
    pinned core revision and compatibility record. There is no release version
    matrix to consume yet.
  </p>
</section>
